# Forge harness

- Workspace is the **super-repo**. Code lives in git submodules; agent memory lives in the **memory-repo** submodule at `.ai/memory/` (`memoryRoot = .ai/memory/<submodulePath>/`). Optional **group** docs live at `.ai/memory/groups/<groupId>/` (shared marketing/personas/competitive/principles); `forge.json.group` links a product to that family. Events take a **target**: group id or product (submodule path / cwd). Group target → one plan across members; product target → one repo (still reads `groupRoot` when the product is a member).
- **Board/SCM wins.** Memory is a projection. On discrepancy, update memory — do not "fix" the board to match memory.
- Every event/command starts with **resolve-paths** → **resolve-config**, except: `/forge.sync-schedule` (harness-wide calendar meetings; skip path/memory); `/forge.implement-ticket` and `/forge.validate-ticket` (skip `sync-memory` / memory Apply / `commit-memory`; still resolve-paths + resolve-config). Path ambiguity is a hard stop. For pausing events, **skip `sync-memory` until Accept** (Plan cannot pull); Apply runs `sync-memory` first and fails closed if pulled files diverge from the accepted plan. Memory-repo sync failure is a hard stop for events that Apply memory. For implement/validate, memory-repo sync failure is not a stop.
- Event commands are the parent: spawn listed agents as **propose-only** subagents; parent merges, presents a **plan delta** (Cursor Plan Mode when available; markdown otherwise), then on **Accept** Validates and Applies (vendor/SCM first, then memory, then **commit-memory** push to memory-repo `main`). After the plan exists: **Accept (build)** Applies the whole plan; **conversationally adjust** reshapes and shows a new whole plan; **Cancel** Applies nothing. No partial Apply. Never Apply a plan the user has not accepted as a whole. See README Plan shape.
- **Automation exceptions:** `/forge.implement-ticket` and `/forge.validate-ticket` auto-Apply vendor/SCM only (no Plan pause, no memory). Validate auto-merges on dual QA + Security approve, then deletes the source branch and moves the board to Done. Pass-back posts a FAIL PR comment and leaves the card In Review.
- Memory-repo is agent-owned git: **no branches, no PRs/MRs** — commit and push `main` only. Subagents do not Apply, do not pause with the orchestrator, and do not mutate SCM unless executing parent-accepted Apply steps (or parent auto-Apply on implement/validate).
- Doc templates: all seeded memory docs use YAML frontmatter schemas (`doc: <role>.*`, `schema_version: 1`); body is expansion-only (empty OK at init). Bump `updated` when frontmatter changes. Current state only — no changelogs or dated decision logs in body. Group-owned docs (when `forge.json.group` is set): `marketing/*`, `product/personas.md`, `product/competitive.md`, `design/principles.md` under `groups/<id>/`. Standalone products keep those under `memoryRoot`. `kind: site` seeds brief + design only (no board/engineering seed).
- Orientation: run `/forge.help`. New project: ensure `.ai/memory` submodule → `/forge.init-project` → `/forge.roadmap-review` → large ideas via `/forge.new-initiative` → HLD (`/forge.initiative-design`, `/forge.initiative-planning`) → LLD (`/forge.backlog-grooming` → `/forge.refinement`) (see README New project path). Icebox still holds coarse outcomes; initiatives are separate from Icebox tickets.
- Board path: **Initiative HLD** (`initiatives/<slug>/`, status `hld` → sign-offs green in `/forge.initiative-planning` → `lld`) → **Grooming (LLD)** splits initiative into actionable tickets on **Refinement** (one host milestone per initiative; Intention + AC; Designer triage for likely user-facing) → **`/forge.refinement` → Ready** (compile ticket `.feature` into Intention + AC; product contract in issue body for all tickets; **`ai-ready` only** — Architect + Security tech spec comment with `<!-- forge-tech-spec -->` sliced from HLD `spec.md`; `human-ready` body-only is OK; **`ai-ready` means the agent finishes the ticket start to finish** — leftover human executor steps become a separate `human-ready` issue). For **user-facing** tickets, Designer attends and enriches Scope/AC/Verification inline (Figma refs, states, a11y); Ready gate includes **design: pass/fail/N/A** and **structure: pass/fail/N/A** (N/A when non-user-facing). For user-facing **`ai-ready`**, design/structure fail when theme unbound/stale, MCP blocked, ticket lacks frames/states/a11y, or `design-structure-check` reports missing required pages/variable naming patterns/component categories (structure is naming/organization; values stay per-app). When the last initiative ticket goes Ready, mark initiative `status: executing`. `/forge.implement-ticket` only takes Ready + `ai-ready`; requires body + tech spec comment; **all sibling tickets on the initiative milestone must be Ready** before claim; claims **In Progress** immediately after the gate; waits for CI after the PR/MR exists; moves to **In Review** only when CI has succeeded (or the host has no CI). `/forge.validate-ticket` dual approve → auto-merge → delete source branch → **Done** (pass-back stays In Review).
- Optional `/forge.sync-schedule` can mirror Weekly/Biweekly/Monthly rituals to Google Calendar meetings (busy blocks with Google Meet) when MCP is available — not required; never auto-starts events.
- Tickets are actionable only — never create epic/umbrella issues; **initiatives** replace epics (memory + one host milestone per initiative in LLD). Outside initiatives, use a host milestone when grouping **5+** related tickets.
- Skill folder names are unique; see [docs/skill-naming.md](docs/skill-naming.md).
